dcb@wdl1.wdl.loral.com (David C Blume) writes:
>IT REALLY DOES MAKE SENSE TO CONFIRM STEPPING INTO A POOL FROM DRY LAND.
>AND CLEAR THE TYPE-AHEAD BUFFER BEFORE PROMPTING THE USER!
>LET'S ADD THESE SAFEGUARD, PLEASE.
>
	I would like to add that the game should prompt the user in any case
where a particular move would be guaranteed to result in hir death.  I would
like to take exception to instances where the player would have no idea about
the impending death, such as getting bopped by the drawbridge, or in cases
where there is a chance for survival, such as stepping into a pit with <5 hp.
	With respect to pools, perhaps it would be a good idea to give the
player one turn to do something before drowning--attempt a teleport, zap a
wand of fire, etc.  After all, even if you're sinking like a rock, you're not
going to drown instantly, even if you didn't bother to hold your breath.
	Finally, I would like to add a resounding "YES!! YES!! YES!!" to the
idea of clearing the type-ahead buffer before prompting the user.
